# Crag: boot-success watchdog (docs/05 §4). A boot that starts dinit but
# never reaches the boot-success milestone would otherwise sit forever and
# never consume its bootloader attempt counters — this timer forces the
# reboot so the AD-009/AD-008 fallback logic can do its job (3 attempts,
# then the other slot). Timeout default 300 s; override via
# /data/.crag/boot-watchdog-timeout (board/test configurable).
# Only armed on A/B boots (rauc.slot= present on the kernel cmdline).
# Scripted: the start command detaches the watcher (setsid) and returns,
# so the service is simply STARTED and no process-exit bookkeeping can
# surface as a failure.

type = scripted
command = /usr/lib/crag/boot-watchdog.sh
depends-on: early-fs-local.target
